{"case": {"question": "Which required Data Science course may be waived, and what materials must be submitted for review according to the general FAQ?", "answerable": true, "expected_answer_points": ["Only DS-GA 1002 among the required Data Science courses may be waived.", "Submit undergraduate or graduate transcripts, highlighting the relevant courses and grades, and the relevant course syllabi for review; transcripts and syllabi must be translated."]}, "scoring_notes": "A course website is optional if available; do not describe it as mandatory.", "answer": {"answer": "Of the required Data Science courses, only DS-GA 1002 may be waived. To have this course waived, students must submit the following materials for review:
- Undergraduate or Graduate Transcripts (must be translated);
- The course(s) used to waive DS-GA 1002 should be highlighted on the transcript, and the grades received should also be highlighted;
- Syllabi of the course(s) used for the waiver (must be translated);
- If available, the course website [1].", "sources": [{"source_id": 1, "file_name": "masters-in-data-science-faq-general.txt", "heading_path": [], "units": {"1": "Title: Master’s in Data Science: FAQ (General) - NYU Center for Data Science", "2": "Source: https://cds.nyu.edu/masters-in-data-science-faq-general/", "3": "Retrieved at (UTC): 2026-09-07T03:25:38.726Z", "4": "Language: English", "6": "Master’s in Data Science: FAQ (General)", "8": "On this page: Academics • Financial • Miscellaneous", "10": "Below you will find a list of frequently asked questions about CDS’ Master’s in Data Science:", "12": "Academics", "13": "Where can I find the Academic Integrity Policy?", "15": "NYU’s academic integrity policy can be found on the NYU Academic Integrity page. NYU’s Statement on Academic Integrity is also posted at Citation Style Guide: NYU Statement on Academic Integrity.", "16": "GSAS’ statement on academic integrity can be found in our GSAS Statement On Academic Integrity.", "18": "What should I do if I have questions about the Academic Integrity policy?", "20": "If you have questions about the academic integrity policy, please reach out to faculty and/or the CDS Director of Administration, Jessica Rosa at jcr253@nyu.edu.", "22": "What citation and data management resources are available to me as a data science student?", "24": "There are several resources that you can reach out to if you have questions about citation and data management. Our library liaison for the Center for Data Science is Vicky Steeves: vicky.steeves@NYU.edu. A link to her Data Citation workshop presentation can be found on the Citing and Being Cited page.", "26": "A data management guide can be found on our Data Management Planning page.", "27": "A citation guide can be found at our Citation Style Guide home page.", "29": "Are students required to take courses every semester?", "31": "Students are required to be continuously enrolled every fall and spring semester. If there is a semester where you do not want to take courses, please reach out to CDS-masters@nyu.edu to discuss options. This requirement does not apply to the summer semester.", "33": "What is a full-time course load for CDS students? What is a part-time course load for CDS students?", "35": "Full-time CDS students register for 9 credits. Part-time students register for less than 9 credits.", "37": "What can I expect regarding workload?", "39": "Students should plan on spending 10-15 hours per week per data science course, assuming they have all the prerequisites. The data science courses are graduate-level courses and move extremely quickly, making it difficult to catch up if you fall behind. Use your resources and ask questions!", "41": "Is there a minimum GPA for the program?", "43": "Yes, each semester, students must maintain a minimum GPA of 3.0 and must successfully complete 66% of credits attempted.", "45": "Where can I find the MS in Data Science curriculum?", "47": "This information can be found on our Course Curriculum page.", "49": "What is the process for waiving required data science courses?", "51": "Of the required Data Science courses, only DS-GA 1002 may be waived. Incoming new students will receive information about the waiver process, but generally the following information needs to be submitted and reviewed:", "52": "– Undergraduate or Graduate Transcripts (must be translated);", "53": "– The course(s) that you will be using to waive the required course should be highlighted. The grade(s) you received in the course(s) should be highlighted as well;", "54": "– Syllabi of the course(s) that you will be using to waive the required course (Must be translated);", "55": "– If available, course website", "57": "Where can I find important registration dates (add/drop deadline, late registration start, etc.)?", "59": "The academic calendar will have this information, which you can find on our Academic Calendar page.", "61": "I’m having trouble with Albert and registration. What should I do?", "63": "Registration help guides can be found on the Registering on Albert page. There are guides on add/drop, the swap function, and other important registration steps.", "65": "I want to register for a non-data science course? What should I do?", "67": "Email Tina Lam (tina.lam@NYU.edu) the course information. She will advise on the registration process for that particular department or school.", "69": "Where can I find a list of approved electives for the MSDS program?", "71": "This information can be found on our Course Curriculum page.", "73": "There is a course that I would like to take as an elective for the MSDS program, but it is not on the pre-approved elective list. What should I do?", "75": "(Here is the link to the Pre-Approved elective list for reference.)", "76": "Please complete the Elective Request for DS Students Google Form. You will be asked for the following information:", "77": "– Course information", "78": "– Course syllabus", "79": "– Relevance of the course to your MSDS degree and goals", "80": "– If available, course website", "81": "If you have any questions, please contact Tina Lam (tina.lam@nyu.edu).", "83": "How many independent study (DS-GA 1010) credits can I apply to the MSDS degree?", "85": "MSDS students can apply up to 6 credits of independent study (DS-GA 1010) to the MSDS degree.", "87": "Can I take a course pass/fail and count it towards the MSDS degree?", "89": "Only 1 elective (this does not include the “One Data Science Elective” requirement) and DS-GA 1009 can be taken as pass/fail and count towards the MSDS degree. Students in the Industry Concentration can use their 1 elective allowance for an Industry Concentration elective. Required courses for the degree cannot be taken as pass/fail.", "91": "I will be ready to graduate at the end of this semester. What should I do?", "93": "You will need to apply for graduation during the graduation application period. For information on how to apply and the deadlines, visit the NYU Applying for Graduation page. If you have other questions for this page, please email the CDS MS program contact email: CDS-masters@nyu.edu.", "95": "Financial", "97": "How much does the program cost?", "99": "Tuition and fees for the current academic year can be found on the Graduate School of Arts and Science Tuition and Fees page.", "101": "Does NYU offer financial aid and/or scholarships?", "103": "Please see our Financial Aid page.", "105": "How do I apply for the DeepMind Scholarship or other tuition scholarships?", "107": "CDS offers a limited number of tuition scholarships for our students. All applicants for admission are considered for these awards on a competitive basis. Scholarship recipients will be notified in their admit letter.", "109": "Are paid research/teaching assistant positions available?", "111": "On-campus positions are available at CDS and NYU, but we do not guarantee such opportunities for any given student. Positions are competitive, and are typically posted on a semester-by-semester basis.", "113": "Miscellaneous", "114": "Where else can I learn more about the application process?", "116": "Please visit the GSAS Application Resource page for more FAQs.", "118": "I was accepted into the program, but would like to defer my admission. Is this possible?", "120": "The Center for Data Science will not approve requests for deferral of admission. If an admitted student wishes to delay enrollment, it will be necessary to decline the offer of admission and reapply for admission the following year. A completely new application will be required. The new application will be considered along with all other applications at that later time.", "122": "Are there any internships or volunteer opportunities at CDS?", "124": "The NYU Center for Data Science provides opportunities for CDS students to connect with companies through various career and professional development initiatives. Please see our Student Career & Professional Development page for more information.", "126": "How can I apply for an administrative position at CDS?", "128": "Available administrative positions will be posted on the NYU Careers page."}}, {"source_id": 2, "file_name": "masters-in-data-science-faq.txt", "heading_path": [], "units": {"1": "Copies of your official transcripts should be uploaded with your application. If you are accepted, the Graduate School of Arts & Sciences will request a mailed copy of your transcripts. Please note that only electronic submissions will be accepted in the application. Please see the GSAS Admissions FAQs for more information.", "3": "I am having technical problems with the online application system – who should I contact?", "5": "Please contact GSAS Graduate Enrollment Services at gsas.admissions@nyu.edu.", "7": "What is the application deadline?", "9": "Please visit the NYU GSAS Data Science page.", "11": "I am very interested in the data science program, but I do not have a strong background in math. Can I still apply?", "13": "A strong background in math is not required, but there are prerequisites that should be met – please see the Admissions Requirements page for more information.", "15": "What do I do if one of my references can’t use the online recommendation system?", "17": "Please review the Graduate School of Arts and Science’s FAQ section for the policies regarding letters of recommendation.", "19": "Standardized Testing", "20": "Do I need to take the GRE or GMAT to apply? If so, what scores will be accepted?", "22": "We do not accept GMAT scores. The GRE is optional. For more information regarding the GRE exam, visit the ETS website. Please also see the related GSAS Admissions FAQ section for more information on standardized testing.", "24": "What is the minimum cutoff for GRE, IELTS, and TOEFL?", "26": "Many factors are taken into account by the admissions committee. There is no minimum cutoff for standardized tests. However, for the IELTS, there is a recommended minimum band score of 7.0. For the TOEFL, there is a recommended minimum score of 100 on the internet-based test.", "28": "Is it possible to waive the TOEFL or IELTS?", "30": "The Graduate School requires applicants who are not native English speakers to submit official TOEFL or IELTS score results. The TOEFL/IELTS requirement is waived if your baccalaureate or master’s degree was (or will be) completed at an institution where the language of instruction is English. Please see the related GSAS Admissions FAQ section for more information.", "32": "Financial", "33": "How much does the program cost?", "35": "Tuition and fees for the current academic year can be found on the Graduate School of Arts and Science Tuition and Fees page. The MS in Data Science Program requires 36 course credits.", "37": "Does NYU offer financial aid and/or scholarships?", "39": "Please see our Financial Aid page.", "41": "How do I apply for CDS’s tuition scholarships?", "43": "CDS offers a limited number of tuition scholarships for our students. All applicants for admission are considered for these awards on a competitive basis. There is no separate scholarship application process. Scholarship recipients will be notified in their admit letter.", "45": "Are paid research/teaching assistant positions available?", "47": "On-campus positions are available at CDS and NYU, but we do not guarantee such opportunities for any given student. Positions are competitive, and are typically posted on a semester-by-semester basis.", "49": "Miscellaneous", "50": "Where else can I learn more about the application process?", "52": "Please visit the GSAS Application Resource page for more FAQs.", "54": "I was accepted into the program, but would like to defer my admission. Is this possible?", "56": "The Center for Data Science will not approve requests for deferral of admission. If an admitted student wishes to delay enrollment, it will be necessary to decline the offer of admission and reapply for admission the following year. A completely new application will be required. The new application will be considered along with all other applications at that later time.", "58": "Are there any internships or volunteer opportunities at CDS?", "60": "The NYU Center for Data Science provides opportunities for CDS students to connect with companies through various career and professional development initiatives. Please see our Student Career & Professional Development overview page for more information.", "62": "How can I apply for an administrative position at CDS?", "64": "Available administrative positions will be posted on the NYU Careers page.", "66": "What if my visa is delayed or if I encounter issues securing a visa?", "68": "All visa and immigration related questions should be directed to the NYU Office of Global Services."}}, {"source_id": 3, "file_name": "masters-in-data-science-faq.txt", "heading_path": [], "units": {"1": "Referenced links (linked content is not included unless saved separately):", "2": "MS Program FAQ page — https://cds.nyu.edu/masters-in-data-science-faq-general/", "3": "Master’s Admissions Requirements page — https://cds.nyu.edu/admissions/masters-in-data-science-admissions-req/admissions-requirements/", "4": "PhD Overview page — https://cds.nyu.edu/phd-program-overview/", "5": "NYU GSAS Data Science page — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center/2017-programs--requirements--and-deadlines/data-science.html", "6": "NYU GSAS General Application Policies page — https://as.nyu.edu/departments/sca/current-students/nyu-gsas-general-application-policies.html", "7": "our non-degree program admissions requirements page — https://cds.nyu.edu/non-degree-admissions-requirements/", "8": "GSAS FAQs here — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/arc/academic-transcripts.html", "9": "admissions and educational prerequisites — https://cds.nyu.edu/admissions/masters-in-data-science-admissions-req/admissions-requirements/#prereq", "10": "Curriculum webpage — https://cds.nyu.edu/masters-in-data-science-curriculum/", "11": "Master’s Curriculum page — https://cds.nyu.edu/masters-curriculum/", "12": "the NYU Graduate School of Arts and Science website — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center/faqs/international-students.html", "13": "GSAS Admissions FAQ — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center/faqs/testing-requirements.html#17", "14": "GSAS Admissions FAQ — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center/nyu-gsas-general-application-policies.html#4", "15": "Admissions Requirements — https://cds.nyu.edu/masters-admissions/", "16": "GSAS Admissions FAQs — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center/faqs/academic-transcripts.html", "17": "the Admissions Requirements page — https://cds.nyu.edu/admissions-requirements/", "18": "FAQ section — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center/faqs/letters-of-recommendation.html", "19": "ETS website — https://www.ets.org/gre", "20": "related GSAS Admissions FAQ section — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center/faqs/testing-requirements.html", "21": "GSAS Admissions FAQ section — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center/faqs/testing-requirements.html#2", "22": "GSAS Admissions FAQs — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center/faqs/testing-requirements.html#4", "23": "Graduate School of Arts and Science Tuition and Fees page — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/financial-aid/tuition-fees.html", "24": "Financial Aid page. — https://cds.nyu.edu/masters-in-data-science-financial-aid-fellowships/", "25": "GSAS Application Resource page — https://gsas.nyu.edu/admissions/gsas-application-resource-center.html", "26": "Student Career & Professional Development overview page — https://cds.nyu.edu/student-career-development-professional-development-overview/", "27": "the NYU Careers page — https://www.nyu.edu/about/careers-at-nyu.html", "28": "NYU Office of Global Services — https://www.nyu.edu/students/student-information-and-resources/student-visa-and-immigration.html"}}, {"source_id": 4, "file_name": "admissions-requirements.txt", "heading_path": [], "units": {"1": "Calculus I: limits, derivatives, series, integrals, etc.", "2": "Linear Algebra", "3": "Intro to Computer Science (or an equivalent “CS-101” programming course): We have no set requirements regarding specific languages, but we generally expect serious academic and/or professional experience with Python and/or R at a minimum.", "4": "One of Calculus II, Probability, Statistics, or an advanced physics, engineering, or econometrics course with heavy mathematical content", "6": "Preference is given to applicants with prior exposure to machine learning, computational statistics, data mining, large-scale scientific computing, or operations research (either in an academic or professional context), as well as to applicants with significantly more mathematical and/or computer science training than the minimum requirements listed above.", "8": "Work Experience", "10": "Many of our students join us directly from undergraduate study, but we also very much welcome evidence of relevant work experience—and clear employment goals once the MSDS is completed—in data science.  Past experience and career goals can be related to commercial industry, government, academia, or other sectors.", "12": "Standardized Tests", "14": "The GRE General Test is optional. If submitting, please note: we do not accept “out of date” scores (see Graduate School of Arts and Science’s Test Scores FAQs); nor do we accept scores of other, similar tests.", "16": "If submitting scores for the GRE General test with your application, please upload a PDF of the unofficial scores, which are made available upon completion of your test, to the “Additional Information Section” of your application. This is in addition to sending your official scores to the Graduate School of Arts and Sc